{"/api/discogs/artist/1930772/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1930772","image":"https://i.discogs.com/STjJaCEf1u61732XjT290OgnOggA8bRtPRFBd8sUYnw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5MzA3/NzItMTczOTgwOTU1/NC02NjM1LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/oHzEslWRxQVyEkrbFkhTEx_xSTPxQ7mulE8heEKwMI8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5MzA3/NzItMTczOTgwOTU1/NC02NjM1LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"House DJ/producer from New York City, USA, living in Barcelona, Spain","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1930772","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":15765348,"name":"Ralph Rodriguez (6)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1930772-Ralph-Session","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/ralphsession","https://twitter.com/ralphsession","https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCno7idOmjYCIswEXYs-yF6w","https://www.instagram.com/ralphsession/","https://www.residentadvisor.net/dj/ralphsession","https://ralphsession.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/229071/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"229071","image":"https://i.discogs.com/bt6aLSw0xWinueuht4mmNuxQaG-EYJ8RxLobwaBqJ7c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:332/w:500/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyOTA3/MS0xNjA0MzUzMjE3/LTE4NzMuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/YNLMOXXhhr5yrbx5a5PDBT598_zDeJiqlbdNPEYkAK0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyOTA3/MS0xNjA0MzUzMjE3/LTE4NzMuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Jamaican dancehall artist and entrepreneur, born January 7, 1976 in Kingston.\r\n\r\nGrowing up in Portmore, he would practice with neighborhood sound systems Soul Signal and Electric Force, and in 1993, Adijah, in his late teens, recorded his first single \"Love Fat Woman\" for Alvin Reid's [l=One Heart] label under the name Adi Banton, a name he chose in tribute to [a=Buju Banton] who was one of his role models.\r\n\r\nHe recorded several more tracks for local producers until 1996 when he and two friends, Mr. Lee and a singer called Escobar, decided to form a group. After watching a movie about Pablo Escobar and his infamous cartel, Adijah came up with a name for his trio: Vibes Cartel. The group soon broke up due to internal frictions leaving Adijah to continue alone. He chose to keep the name of the group changing the C to K in Kartel and adopting the moniker Vybz Kartel.\r\n\r\nIn 1998, after performing at the Champions In Action stage show in his hometown of Portmore, Vybz linked up with [a=Bounty Killer]. His new role as Killer’s protégé attracted attention from the public, and he progressed to collaborations with Bounty Killer. He then released on his own hits and collaborated with other artists. This led to a deal with UK/US based label [l=Greensleeves Records].\r\n\r\nOn April 3, 2014, Kartel was sentenced to life in prison for the murder of Clive 'Lizard' Williams in August 2011. He continued to release music while in prison by recording vocals in his cell, into an iPhone, with a beat playing on an iPad. These vocals were then sent to engineer [a=Mario Antonia Dunwell] aka [a=Dunw3ll] and producer [a=Linton \"TJ\" White]. On July 31, 2024, after 12 years 10 months in prison, Kartel and his three co-defendants were freed.\r\n\r\nFather of [a3885536].\r\nCommon-law husband of [a4959236].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:229071","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":575402,"name":"Adidja Palmer"},{"id":3555103,"name":"Worl' Boss"},{"id":5157684,"name":"Addi Innocent"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["A. Palmer","Addi","Addi Di Teacha","Cartel","Kartel","Mr Vybz Kartel","V. Kartel","V.Kartel","VK","VYBZ","VYBZ Cartel","VYBZ Karte","VYBZ Kartel","VYBZ Kartell","VYbz Kartel","Vbyz Kartel","Vibes","Vibes Cartel","Vibes Kartel","Vibez Cartel","Vibez Kartel","Vibz Cartel","Vibz Cartell","Vibz Kartel","Vibze Cartel","Vives Kartel","Vybes Cartel","Vybes Cartell","Vybes Kartel","Vybez Cartel","Vybez Kart","Vybez Kartel","Vybez kartel","Vybs Kartel","Vybz","Vybz Cartel","Vybz Cartell","Vybz Kartal","Vybz Karte","Vybz Kartel And Friends","Vybz Kartell","Vybz Katel","Vybz Palmer","VybzKartel","Vyvz","Vyzb Cartel","Vyzb Kartel","V· Kartel"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/229071-Vybz-Kartel","type":"artist","urls":["https://x.com/Vybz_Kartel","https://www.facebook.com/p/Vybzkartel-100044264687653/","https://www.instagram.com/vybzkartel/","https://soundcloud.com/vybz-kartel-5","https://www.youtube.com/user/VybzKartelVEVO","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vybz_Kartel"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/267474/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"267474","image":"https://i.discogs.com/yAGFnfHkL0IU4f4gXuOu02hbH-7UF9x71M-T1qbanag/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:480/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI2NzQ3/NC0xNzMwOTk3NjU4/LTQyMTAuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/LB4jb3rvGiLI6ziRHtFjID8NstwLf5Yj9wQP4tcNlhk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI2NzQ3/NC0xNzMwOTk3NjU4/LTQyMTAuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Producer from UK.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:267474","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1488540,"name":"Stephen James Wilkinson"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["81810","ビビオ"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/267474-Bibio","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.bibio.co","http://www.facebook.com/mrBibio","http://bibio.bleepstores.com","http://twitter.com/Bibio","http://soundcloud.com/bibio","http://warp.net/artists/bibio","http://www.flickr.com/photos/33701035@N00","http://vimeo.com/mrbibio","http://www.youtube.com/user/mrbibio","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibio","https://bibio.bandcamp.com/","http://www.myspace.com/mrbibio"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2989601/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2989601","image":"https://i.discogs.com/BJ5svWamTeXigNWKMsA5VImFugb_mkwSFNXzMoS7MJY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:376/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5ODk2/MDEtMTU2ODI0NjUy/Ni02NDAyLnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/iGvjiITTjnMzIM2ev_xYlfPILkUMogqLkARtwj9Addo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5ODk2/MDEtMTU2ODI0NjUy/Ni02NDAyLnBuZw.jpeg","profile":"Chen Fen-Lan (born 1948 in Tainan, Taiwan) is a Taiwanese pop singer who recorded in both Mandarin and Taiwanese. Known as \"Taiwan's Hibari Misora,\" she began her career at the age of eight with her hit debut record Gū-Lú Ê Guān-Bāng (The Orphan Girl's Wish).\n\nAt 14, she moved to Japan to pursue her music career, becoming the first singer from Taiwan to enter the Japanese music industry. She is the original singer of the legendary classic The Moon Represents My Heart (月亮代表我的心). Another of her signature hits is the lively Taiwanese song Pleasant Sailing (快樂的出帆), whose hopeful lyrics capture Taiwan's vibrant maritime spirit and have been covered by numerous female artists.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2989601","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Chen Fern Lan","Miss Fen-Lan Cheng","陳芬兰","陳芬蘭","陳芳蘭"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2989601-Chen-Fen-Lan","type":"artist","urls":["https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-tw/陳芬蘭"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3753436/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3753436","image":"https://i.discogs.com/-yIqFt0eOe15165AvkDqjueS02QHNZFfc9_F8gU7ETA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3NTM0/MzYtMTU4OTI5NDU3/NC0yNzE3LnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/ohHerYOms98QR6yeGePjc7cyAVvDlPCnpwF_pZE9AOg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3NTM0/MzYtMTU4OTI5NDU3/NC0yNzE3LnBuZw.jpeg","profile":"DJ and producer from Australia. Founder of [l1704565].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3753436","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":15898985,"name":"Thomas Martin (23)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["F. Frank","F.Frank","Frank"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3753436-Furious-Frank","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/Furious-Frank-1055141617862738","https://soundcloud.com/furiousfrank"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4091/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4091","image":"https://i.discogs.com/-VX--C0HsKgb3X2BrpSBn_3_2DSUsUQrpu5c-Zj9ouE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:383/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQwOTEt/MTY3OTQ3MzE4OS02/OTY5LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/ytUN2J65_XgJkVWT-ym8O2hhrIxUsHjNL7a8-Va6XMk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQwOTEt/MTY3OTQ3MzE4OS02/OTY5LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"De La Soul is an American hip-hop trio of Posdnuos, Trugoy, and Maseo, formed in 1987 in the Amityville area of Long Island, New York. They are best known for their eclectic sampling, quirky lyrics, and contributions to the evolution of jazz rap and alternative hip-hop subgenres. The three formed the group in high school, catching the attention of producer Prince Paul with a demo tape of the song \"Plug Tunin'.\" With its playful wordplay, innovative sampling, and witty skits, the band's debut album, '3 Feet High and Rising', has been called \"a hip-hop masterpiece.\"  \r\nThey are original members of the progressive collective known as the [a=Native Tongues], which includes [a=A Tribe Called Quest], [a=Queen Latifah], [a=Black Sheep], [a=Monie Love], and founding members the [a=Jungle Brothers]. Their output throughout the '90s, 1991's 'De La Soul Is Dead,' 1993's 'Buhoone Mindstate' and 1996's 'Stakes Is High,' while not as commercially successful as their debut, were all formative for hip-hop and are now widely considered cult classics. \r\nAfter 2004's critically acclaimed 'The Grind Date,' and winning a Grammy for their collaboration with [a=Gorillaz] on their single \"Feel Good Inc.\" in 2006, De La Soul went on hiatus sans a few singles and an EP, returning in 2016 with the crowd-funded 'And the Anonymous Nobody.' In 2023, after years of legal battles over rights and ownership, De La Soul regained access to their back catalog from [a=Tommy Boy Records] and finally released their classic albums on streaming services and new reissues for the first time. Unfortunately, it was bittersweet after the death of original member Dave 'Trugoy' Jolicoeur, days before the release. Jolicoeur passed away at 54 after suffering from congestive heart failure diagnosed in 2017. \r\nIndustry rumors suggest an untitled tenth album may be released with production from [a=Pete Rock] and [a=DJ Premier]. \r\nIndividual aliases:\r\n[a=Dave Jolicoeur] AKA [a=Trugoy The Dove] / Plug Two / [a=Plug 2]\r\n[a=Kelvin Mercer] AKA [a=Posdnuos] / [a=Plug Won] / [a=Plug 1]\r\n[a=Vincent Mason] AKA [a=Pasemaster Mase] / [a=Maseo] / Plug Three\r\n\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4091","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":89975,"name":"Dave Jolicoeur"},{"active":true,"id":297026,"name":"Kelvin Mercer"},{"active":true,"id":318912,"name":"Vincent Mason"}],"namevariations":["D.L.S.","DLS","Da La Soul","De La","De La Sou","DeLa Soul","DeLaSoul","Del La Soul","Dela Soul","DelaSoul","Delasoul","Della Soul","The Dela Soul Sound"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4091-De-La-Soul","type":"artist","urls":["http://wearedelasoul.com","http://www.allmusic.com/artist/de-la-soul-mn0000238322","http://delasoul.bandcamp.com","http://www.facebook.com/wearedelasoul","http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0857252","https://www.instagram.com/wearedelasoul/","http://www.last.fm/music/De+La+Soul?ac=de%20la%20so","http://www.myspace.com/delasoul","http://www.songkick.com/artists/73301","http://soundcloud.com/wearedelasoul","http://wearedelasoul.tumblr.com","http://twitter.com/wearedelasoul","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_La_Soul","http://www.youtube.com/delasolarsystem"]}},"/api/discogs/artist